Z||000000||fiero56||11-29-1999||04:12 PM||||I was driving down 48 yesterday afternoon, and just past the intersection for Spring Valley I saw in the parking lot in front of the Pizza Hut/Dairy Queen lineup a white '84-'86 coupe.  It had the base bumper pads and the gold badge up front from '84-'85. But, the car also had the fastback sail panels, tail-lights, and ground effects. Although it had the fastback taillights, it still had the lower rear fascia with the bumper pads.  It looked real cool.  Instead of the regular taillights it had a different set on it.  Two big circles and nothing else, just black covers. I did a circle around it in the lot, but alas, I wasn't in my Fiero so I didn't stop and see who owned it.  Anybody ever think of this combination.  If I see it today I'll snag a picture with my digital camera and post it.||||reg||7
